  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gap Analysis for Health Genomics Ecosystem in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to understand the existing gaps in the current Indonesia national genomics initiatives and benchmark against global best practices, standards and regulations in the genomics space including the following scopes:
- Comparison with other international jurisdictions
- Benchmarking BGSi&#x2019;s genomic services with international standards using levers and sub-levers, and with focus on policy/regulation and operational aspects
- Determining current gaps in Indonesia&#x2019;s genomics ecosystem and best practices in implementing national genomics initiatives
- To provide recommendations on action plan to align with global best practices.

The anticipated outcomes of these projects aim to bolster the genomics landscape and its associated parties in Indonesia. This will be achieved by pinpointing existing gaps and determining actionable steps that can be taken to advance genomic efforts within the nation.</narrative>
  </description>
